    "notes": "The three handlers are gated by a caller-UID comparison with ACCESSTOKEN_UID, which this file's own sources bind to the reviewed value 3020, and each call is one of the three operations the reviewed record says that account authorizes. The role is credited for those operations only, so the three candidates are not raised. Under the default policy the account assignment is unreviewed, so `ipc.auth.missing` is raised at the three call sites: this row asserts that, and is therefore a positive control, not a fixed one. The three candidates are held back only for a harness that supplies the reviewed policy explicitly -- see policy_context. A `fixed` label here would have stated the opposite of what the row asserts, and no test reads `variant`, so the mismatch would have been invisible.",
